@@ -334,6 +334,7 @@ Every `test_*.py` file is listed below, with the reason the module exists rather
 | [`test_stage1_browser_fixture.py`](test_stage1_browser_fixture.py) | Builds the browser acceptance's local metadata readiness fixture and uses the production Store, Artifact manager, and completion-delivery verifier to seed 100 atomic deliveries plus same-head/head-change and delegated-producer evidence. Focused tests keep the seed path deterministic, scoped, and free of LLM/network calls. |
 | [`test_server_execution_coordinator.py`](test_server_execution_coordinator.py) | Admission and cancellation on the Web side. Cancellation without an exact execution and owner identity fails closed; it must never fall back to cancelling whatever happens to be running. A queued REPL cancel cannot touch the active Agent. |
 | [`test_session_sidebar_scope.py`](test_session_sidebar_scope.py) | Whether a project's sessions are visible when you open that project. `loadSessions` fetched `/frames?limit=100` **globally** and filtered by project in the browser, so a project whose sessions sat outside that page appeared empty — and `openProject` reads empty as a reason to call `newSession()`, presenting a blank session to a user whose work was intact in SQLite. Measured: 120 sessions in one project push a three-session project entirely out of the global page; 0 of 3 visible before, 3 of 3 after, confirmed again in a real browser. The server has supported `project_id`, cursors and `next_cursor` the whole time — this was one unused query parameter. |
+| [`test_session_list_folder_id.py`](test_session_list_folder_id.py) | Whether a session moved into a folder shows up inside it. `browse_frames` selected an explicit column list without `folder_id`, and `_frame_json` reads the key with `.get`, so every `GET /frames` row answered `folder_id: null` while `POST /frames/{id}/folder` had succeeded and SQLite held the right value. The sidebar groups by that field, so a folder always counted zero and its sessions fell into the date buckets — confirmed in a real browser through the sidebar's own "Move to folder" menu. Pins the repository row, the route row on a real socket (unmarked, so the response-schema capture records `frames[].folder_id` as a string), and the general form: for a session with every root field set, its list row reports each field the detail route reports, identically. |
 | [`test_session_and_message_paging.py`](test_session_and_message_paging.py) | Reaching the part of a project, and of a conversation, that is off the page. Walks the session-list keyset cursor across 260 sessions and the message cursor back through 640, asserting no gap, no duplicate, and that a session or message arriving mid-walk does not shift a later page. Pins the two page-size defects the walk exposed: `?limit=banana` reached the browser as a 500 `internal_error` while the same route already answered 400 for `before_seq=banana`, and `?limit=-5` answered 200 with an empty page and `has_earlier: false` — the exact shape of "you have reached the beginning". Exercises the session package export end to end: first message, last message, and a forked branch's own message, with every `message_id` still attached to its own row. |
 | [`test_session_branching.py`](test_session_branching.py) | Four tests on checkpoint, fork, revert, and undo. Revert preview reports every state dimension without writing anything, and an external edit to the workspace blocks the revert and is recorded instead of being overwritten. |
 | [`test_session_control_tools.py`](test_session_control_tools.py) | The current-session and capability tools. Capability search is always visible and activates the session group, approval inputs are redacted through the dispatcher, and a mutation fails closed when the domain it needs is not filesystem-aware. |
